Z||000009||theogre||03-20-2000||09:05 PM||||This is important in any car to watch for but especialy important with Fiero with it's transverse catalyst setup the way it is. I thought of exactly this happening when I had to run over a plastic bag tonight. Fortunatly it didn't hang up on me.<P>I have to get under mine as soon as I get a warm day again and change the fuel filter. I'll have a good look and see if there's a way to make a guard for the catalyst the won't block the air movement. Maybe a section of expanded steel would work.||||reg||1
Z||000010||ROB MAC||03-21-2000||09:20 PM||||Did I say my first "instinct" was to run? I admit I did run but I went back and saved it.It's O.K. if you want to take back the C.P.C. award I'll understand but whats important is the Fiero still swings.||||reg||1
Z||000011||FIEROCIOUS||03-22-2000||11:17 PM||||I dragged a tumbble weed under my car for three days! Guess how I know it was under there for three days?......<P>My wife as I pull it out from under my car says "That been under there since tues."<P>I looked at her like (Hmm I wonder if she thought it should be under there?)<BR>You know what she said?.......<P>"Why did you put that under there?"<P>She has her moments! I love her just the same!||||reg||1
